ructured_run).\n\nSplit executed as a pure refactor — moved code is byte-identical, only module headers/imports differ:\n- src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py (205 LOC): FailureContext, interpret_failure, _write_parse_failure_artifact\n- src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py (248 LOC): warn_if_cache_ineffective, cache_write_never_read, warn_if_cache_write_never_read, estimate_marked_prefix_tokens, _warn_if_zeroed_usage\n- src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py: 796 -> 436 LOC (run mechanism only), with an explicit __all__ re-exporting every moved name so no caller or test changed.\n\nLocal gates green so far: make lint (ruff check + format + complexity-baseline --check: active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0 — baseline unchanged, no regeneration needed), make typecheck (mypy 520 files clean), all check_* gates, generators no-diff, and the 100 oracle tests across test_structured_run_seam / test_interpret_failure_seam / test_cache_floor_warning / test_cache_floor_per_model / test_cache_prefix_breakpoint / test_settings_builders_seam / test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019 / test_structured_run / test_module_size_contract. Full CI suite running.","timestamp":1786598352706654001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 1707 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1707), local commit ed3146a254.\n\nFull local gate set green before push: make lint (ruff check + format-check + complexity-baseline --check, active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0 — the baseline file is UNCHANGED, so no regeneration was needed), make typecheck (mypy, 520 files, clean), all check_* gates (adr_numbers, comment_hygiene, config_reads, docs_index, raw_git_writes, readme_quickstart, server_manifest, verify_gate_parity, wall_clock_asserts; build_env_locked/complexity_baseline are CI-arg-driven and were exercised via make lint), the four generators (gen_adr_index/gen_cli_reference/gen_env_registry/gen_mcp_reference) with no diff, and the CI suite: 12621 passed, 52 skipped, exit 0.\n\nEnvironment note for the epic: the first two full-suite attempts died in xdist teardown ('OSError: cannot send (already closed?)' across all three workers, no summary line) because five sibling implementer suites were running concurrently on this host — load average peaked at ~27. Re-running detached once load dropped gave a clean 12621-passed run. Worth flagging to the CI-flake child fade-ea90: the failure signature matches, and host memory/CPU contention reproduces it locally.","timestamp":1786601543523528001}],"created_at":1786219928966181001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5469f149-ade4-4790-badf-c75815c6ee32","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5536-a55c-ab74-4428"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` is 796 LOC — 4 under the 800 hard cap enforced by the CI module-size gate (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so any addition turns the build red. It grew because a single module accreted THREE distinct responsibilities: the run mechanism, cache-effectiveness *diagnostics*, and *failure interpretation*. Zero in-progress file_impact contention. Flagged by audit ae1b.\n\n## Approach\nDecompose by responsibility (not by line count) into three cohesive modules with a one-way dependency direction — the recurrence-preventing fix: future cache-warning or failure-classification logic then lands in its own module instead of re-inflating the orchestrator.\n\n1. Extract the **cache-effectiveness diagnostics** cluster → new `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py` (~230 LOC): `warn_if_cache_ineffective` (structured_run.py:533), `cache_write_never_read` (:645), `warn_if_cache_write_never_read` (:675), `estimate_marked_prefix_tokens` (:704), `_warn_if_zeroed_usage` (:740).\n2. Extract the **failure-interpretation** cluster → new `src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py` (~180 LOC): `FailureContext` (:45), `interpret_failure` (:59), `_write_parse_failure_artifact` (:304).\n3. `structured_run.py` retains the run mechanism (`_pai_structured` :186, `build_model_settings` :342, `build_usage_limits` :420, `effective_max_iterations` :461, `_known_model_output_ceiling` :470, `effective_max_tokens` :489, `_extract_usage` :499, `_import_pydantic_ai` :764, `_pai_check_config` :775) → ~390 LOC.\n\nRationale (G6): responsibility-based seams are stable, so the split does not need to be redone as code evolves; the two extracted modules are pure/observability code with no back-edge into the orchestrator. **Preserve every public import path** by re-exporting the moved names from `structured_run.py` (`from .run_failure import FailureContext, interpret_failure` etc.) — external importers `llm/runner.py`, `llm/usage_report.py`, `llm/capabilities.py` docs, and the tests are then untouched, keeping the edit-set non-overlapping. The re-export also keeps `test_structured_run_seam.py::test_moved_symbols_are_importable_from_the_new_module` (which asserts `hasattr(structured_run, \"_warn_if_zeroed_usage\")`) green with no test edit.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` — remove the two extracted clusters; add re-export shims.\n- `src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py` — NEW (cache-effectiveness diagnostics).\n- `src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py` — NEW (failure interpretation + parse-failure artifact).\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor — no new behavior)\n- Moved code is byte-identical; only imports are adjusted. No test edits.\n- `mypy`, ruff, and the module-size gate stay green; `structured_run.py` ≤ 500 LOC; both new modules ≥ 100 LOC.\n- Existing oracle tests pass unchanged: `tests/unit/test_structured_run_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_interpret_failure_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_warning.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_per_model.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py`, `tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` ≤ 500; each new sibling ≥ 100 LOC.\n- [ ] `cache_diagnostics.py` and `run_failure.py` contain exactly the named symbols; neither imports back from `structured_run.py`, and neither imports `runner` at runtime.\n- [ ] All prior external import paths still resolve (verified: `python -c \"import rebar.llm.structured_run as s; s.interpret_failure; s.FailureContext; s.build_model_settings; s.warn_if_cache_ineffective; s.warn_if_cache_write_never_read; s._warn_if_zeroed_usage; s.estimate_marked_prefix_tokens\"`).\n- [ ] The full default suite and the module-size/complexity/type/lint gates are green with no test edits required.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"remove two extracted clusters; add re-export shims for moved public names"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/cache_diagnostics.py","reason":"NEW: cache-effectiveness diagnostics cluster"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py","reason":"NEW: failure interpretation + parse-failure artifact"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07"],["relates_to","5536-a55c-ab74-4428"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","parent_status_uuid":"9b5aca61-37f7-461e-8a25-2f7be8195be1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["remediation","file-size","ae1b"],"ticket_id":"5652-1949-3c0a-4b50","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split near-cap module structured_run.py (795 LOC) below the 500-LOC target","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["538e0379-be50-40fa-a265-e610c515a056","0a6116cb-b967-4d07-b26b-251b0c077b83","dd2ae46a-005a-4983-909b-d2752d21867e","15942ac3-4ec4-477e-9b45-907fa4909810","130c89d3-6ee6-46c3-9019-d6d60ef29da3","c6c53bd6-87d1-424c-8963-a563cf4b389c","278a2217-d40b-404d-bc41-69ddaf0aa8f1","9b5aca61-37f7-461e-8a25-